WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande…

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:15.570
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.370
Hiun City, Isshu Region

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.030
Come on out, Lucario!

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.300
Aceburn!

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.790
Satoshi and Go
have arrived at Hiun City, in Isshu.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.560
And as for why they’re here...

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.530
All right, everyone!
Are your bellies ready?!

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.540
Yeah!

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.700
Then...

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.150
My prize for winning
the Pokémon Eating Contest,

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.270
the Isshu all-you-can-eat
gourmet food tour, starts now!

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.900
First, let’s go get some of Isshu’s
famous Hiun Ice Cream!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.590
Let’s go, Aceburn.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.570
Thank you very much.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.470
Hurry up and get here, brat boy.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.160
He’ll never expect that Team Rocket
got here first and are lying in wai—

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.690
While he has his guard down on his
Isshu all-you-can-eat gourmet food tour,

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.330
we’ll quickly snatch Pikachu from him!

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.780
Today’s plan is bound to go well, meow!

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.380
Since this time we have... this, meow!

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.330
This is the Pretty-Much-Pikachu!

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.070
Pretty-Much-Pikachu?

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:49.300
It’s a mech with the exact same appearance,
feel, and temperature of a real Pikachu, meow!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.940
If we secretly switch out the real Pikachu
with this Pretty-Much-Pikachu...

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:02.820
We can get Pikachu
without the brat boys noticing!

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.210
We got Pikachu!

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.230
Huh?

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:17.430
H-Hey, hold on, didn’t this just say
“<i>Hikachu</i>” instead of “Pikachu”?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.330
No, it couldn’t have...

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.720
It did!

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.990
It’s clearly saying “Hikachu”!
It said “Hikahika”!

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.660
What’s the meaning of this, Nyarth?!

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:36.560
To tell the truth, its cry was the one and only thing
I couldn’t replicate, meow…

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.420
So that’s why it’s called
a “Pretty-Much” Pikachu, huh?

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.930
Well, everything else about it
is pretty much a Pikachu...

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.800
Yeah! That dumb brat boy
won’t even notice any difference!

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.910
Right!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:52.930
Excuse me!

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:53.980
That voice...

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.480
I’d like a Hiun Ice Cream!

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.480
C-C-Coming right up!

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.550
Thanks for your continued patronage!

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.910
You’re very lucky customers!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.400
Today’s the anniversary of Hiun Ice Cream!

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.320
So, I’ll add on a
bonus topping for you!

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.310
Great!

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:12.850
Oh, I don’t need any.
I’m fine with plain vanilla.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.840
Then I’ll take both of our bonuses!

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.170
Sure!

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.930
Thank you!

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.310
He fell right in the trap, meow!

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:33.100
While he’s struggling to manage
that hard-to-eat ice cream...

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:37.100
We’ll carry out “Operation:
Swap Pikachu and Pretty-Much Pikachu,” meow!

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.790
You want one, Aceburn?

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.940
You want one, right, Lucario?

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.490
Huh? You don’t?

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.240
Okay, here you go!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:50.930
Here.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.280
Let’s sit down and eat them.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.980
Thank you!

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.770
<i>What a great feeling!</i>

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.220
Delicious!

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.940
Hold on a sec, Pikachu.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:21.810
I know, I know!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.020
Here, Pikachu.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.920
Your hands are all sticky!
Go wash them!

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:02.860
Right.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.430
Okay, hold this.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.150
Hurry back, okay?

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:08.990
Yeah!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.350
Here’s our chance...

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:19.460
All right!

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.710
Looking good, he hasn’t noticed!

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:31.420
Now to grab the real one...

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.850
D-D-Did he catch us?
O-Or see us?

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.130
What’s with Satoshi’s ice cream?!

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:40.980
It keeps melting!

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:47.360
Gah, what are you doing, Satoshi?

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.320
Sheesh!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.950
<i>They’re gone!</i>

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.330
<i>Over there!</i>

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:03.770
Which one’s Pikachu?

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.590
That one! No, that one?

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.890
Listen to the cries, meow!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.190
Hear that?

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.890
That one said “Hikachu”!

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.290
Which means...

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:37.370
This one’s the real Pikachu, meow!

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.640
Look, Go! Sparkling clean!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.610
<i>My</i> hands are all sticky now, though.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:26.000
Hey! Someone’s chasing us!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.550
And now another one?!
T-This isn’t good!

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.310
Try this on for size, meow!

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.320
Geez...

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.590
Sorry, my bad.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.330
Ah, that was great!

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.470
Okay, what do we eat next?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.210
Right...

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:01.890
Huh? Where’s Aceburn and Lucario?

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.070
Haha! We’ve gotta report this
to Sakaki, quick!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:50.000
No way! They stole Pikachu!

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.660
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.610
These are Miruhog Buns,
one of Isshu delicacies!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:24.650
Crunchy fried batter decorated
with mustard for Miruhog’s stripes!

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:27.370
It even has a toothpick for the tail!

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.930
Let’s eat!

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:34.780
It’s great!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:39.630
What’s keeping Aceburn and Lucario, though?

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:46.520
Hey, hold it, meooooooow!

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:48.570
Give Pikachu back!

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.610
Now you can’t get away!

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.580
What’s up with them?

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.820
Let’s just get Pikachu back for now, meow.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.920
They went that far?!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.160
Follow them!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.580
Roger!

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.990
Where’d they go, meow?

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.970
That’s my Pikachu...!

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:33.290
What?

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.210
Ta-daah!

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:48.820
Here’s another Isshu delicacy,
Iwapalace Cake!

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:50.340
It looks great!

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:56.340
Alternating layers of chocolate sponge
and cheesecake, with a <i>sweet</i> coating!

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:59.220
It’s a cake that’ll fill you
all the way up!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:04.650
By the way, apparently
there’s a bite-size Ishizumai cake too!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:05.730
Whoa!

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.580
Now then...

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.110
Let’s dig in!

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:14.630
This Iwapalace cake is the best!

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:25.450
Where did Aceburn and Lucario go?

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:30.140
Maybe they found something tasty and
stuffed themselves till they couldn’t move!

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.640
Give up already...

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.400
Hand over Pikachu!

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:50.230
Glare all you want,
we aren’t scared of you!

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:55.620
We’re not going to lose
to stretchy bounce Pokémon like you!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.250
Vending, come on!

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.010
Nyarth, go for it!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.960
Right, meow!

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:13.720
Rocket...

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:14.930
Vending...

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:17.720
Secret!

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.020
I wonder, what’ll I get?

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.280
The Karate Pokémon, Dageki!

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:32.490
I wonder, what’ll I get?

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.550
The Judo Pokémon, Nageki!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.420
Go, Dageki! Low Kick!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.500
Nageki! Circle Throw!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:19.410
All right! Because of the stretchy bouncy stuff,
a single attack hits both of them!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.290
They self-destructed, meow.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:51.560
Dageki! Brick Break!

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:53.200
Nageki! Parry Throw!

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.940
Yay!

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:17.410
Don’t they look dumb,
swinging each other around?

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.680
Looks like
it thought of something, meow.

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:26.040
Hmph. Like it even matters!

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:30.020
They can’t battle properly as long as they’re
stuck together with the stretchy bouncy stuff!

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:48.530
What’s that?

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:50.590
It’s swinging it around like crazy...

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:14.280
It powered up the move
with stretchy bounciness?!

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.450
<i>No way!</i>

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:36.580
For a while there,
I really thought this was gonna work.

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:43.660
Huh? No way!
You stole Pikachu back?!

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:56.340
Wait? This is the Pretty-Much-Pikachu?

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:00.150
It really is a good replica, meow.

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:02.200
Now’s not the time for
self-congratulating!

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.130
What an awful feeling!

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.860
I’m stuffed...

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.310
I can’t eat another bite.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:18.550
Same...

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.490
They’re back.

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:35.350
What is it, Aceburn? Lucario?

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.050
Are they hungry or something?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.130
Here, some souvenirs.

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:24.490
They really get on well!

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.760
Yeah!

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:35.640
Aceburn and Lucario, pulled apart
and together by a stretchy bouncy tether.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:39.660
They’ll make for a
stretchy bouncy duo... perhaps.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:51.540
Pikachu!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.420
Utsubot!

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:53.120
Transel!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:53.920
Lugia!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:54.710
Achamo!

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:55.500
Morpeko!

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.210
Koduck!

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.090
Cleffy!

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:57.800
Eevee!

00:21:57.800 --> 00:21:58.550
Ishitsubute!

00:21:58.550 --> 00:21:59.210
Teppouo!

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.130
Onisuzume!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:00.840
Metagross!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:01.880
Subame!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:02.550
Me...

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:03.800
Metamon!

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:20.570
Pikachu!

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:21.400
Usohachi!

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:22.110
Chicorita!

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:22.900
Tamatama!

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:23.660
Mamepato!

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:24.490
Togedemaru!

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:25.240
Lucario!

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.030
Odoshishi!

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:26.830
Seadra!

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:27.450
Laplace!

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:28.290
Starmie!

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:29.080
Miniryu!

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:29.870
Windie!

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:30.580
Iwark!

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:31.410
Kucheat!

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:32.160
Togekiss!

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:32.910
Sleep!

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:33.670
Ptera!

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:34.500
Raikou!

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.250
U'u!

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:36.040
Wooloo!

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:36.840
Ruriri!

00:22:36.840 --> 00:22:37.590
Leafia!

00:22:37.590 --> 00:22:38.380
Armorgaw!

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:39.170
Abagoura!

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:39.960
Latias!

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:40.710
Spear!

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:41.460
Agnome!

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:42.220
Muma!

00:22:42.220 --> 00:22:43.300
Madatsubomi!

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:44.760
Mew!

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:09.620
Now, onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.820
Go!

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:14.580
Why do you have an Eevee, Koharu?

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:16.080
It looks like she’s being chased!

00:23:16.460 --> 00:23:17.040
What?!

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:19.040
Koharu! Go!

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:22.550
Those guys sucked Pokémon up
into a machine!

00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:24.010
Whaaat?!

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:28.380
Don’t worry. I’ll protect you.

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:30.300
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:31.070
Koharu and...

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:33.320
...the Very Mysterious Eevee!
